CHIMERA voice engine (vendored)

Source:  https://github.com/jamesondh/chimera-vocal-synth, crates/chimera,
         commit eeb0c1940d2d52f5f5effdecf3507fe79157f389 (eeb0c19, 2026-11-18)
Author:  Jameson Hodge and the project's contributors
Licence: MIT. LICENSE is the upstream repository's own LICENSE file at that commit, unchanged.

Earlier vendored copy: commit 09fb776 (2026-11-07), now kept as crates/chimera-09fb776 so the
Singer can still sing with it.

What is here: the engine's src/ unchanged, and its manifest rewritten to stand alone (version,
edition and licence written out instead of inherited from the upstream workspace; the
dev-dependency used only by the upstream tests dropped). rustfmt.toml is this fork's: it keeps
`cargo fmt` from reformatting the vendored code.

What is not: the upstream tests and golden fixtures, the examples, the CLI (crates/chimera-cli),
the browser crate (crates/chimera-wasm), the web app, and anything derived from the Children's
Song Dataset (CC BY-NC-SA), which the upstream keeps out of its repository too.

data/ holds two files the upstream ships in public/data/, unchanged:
- cmudict.txt.gz: the CMU Pronouncing Dictionary, under the BSD-style licence in
  data/CMUDICT-LICENSE.txt (Copyright (C) 1993-2015 Carnegie Mellon University). The engine's
  English letter-to-sound uses it to sing lyrics.
- mandarin.txt.gz: Mandarin readings (characters and phrases to pinyin), built by the upstream's
  tools/build-mandarin.ts from mozillazg's pinyin-data and phrase-pinyin-data, under the MIT
  licences in data/MANDARIN-PINYIN-LICENSE.txt. The engine's Mandarin front end uses it to sing
  lyrics written in Chinese characters.
